				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Element): Simplify Webview effect payload construction\n\nRefactor the JSON payload creation logic in `Mountain`'s `CreateEffectForRequest/Webview` module to remove redundant line breaks and align comment formatting. Ensure positional `args` are correctly mapped to named aliases (`viewId`, `viewType`, `title`) for `SkyBridge` consumption.\n\nThis update streamlines the code structure without altering functional behavior, maintaining strict IPC consistency and improving readability while preserving the required PascalCase naming and argument mapping strategies for editor UI effects.",
			"SHA": "87d7300257a6eee7e55b67e633a4ba68d9145196"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T10:41:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Restore debuggability and fix IPC payload shape\n\nSynchronize 11 Element submodules to reverse aggressive minification strategies and resolve a critical bug in the native backend. Cocoon, Output, Wind, and Worker restore full source map generation, revert single-character variable obfuscation, and reformat ESBuild configurations to strict PascalCase naming, ensuring production builds remain debuggable and maintainable.\n\nMountain corrects the `registerView` payload shape by including the required `viewId` key, restoring functionality for extension sidebars that were previously dropping host content due to schema mismatches. Maintain adds recursive JSON array deduplication to ensure build idempotency.\n\nThese changes prioritize developer tooling stability, correct silent failures in the IPC layer, and align the build artifacts with project readability standards while maintaining optimization for production releases.",
			"SHA": "16e66325c50780d70bd532478446b38d3b15154e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T13:38:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 6 submodules for build normalization and release optimization\n\nUpdate six Element submodules to resolve build pipeline inconsistencies, enforce strict PascalCase naming conventions, and optimize production artifacts.\n\nCocoon and Wind refactor ESBuild configurations into modular structures before applying aggressive minification (removing source maps and renaming to single-char identifiers) for release size reduction, while restoring readable, debuggable builds for development. Output follows suit, reformatting its plugin pipeline for readability before minifying entry points and deleting source maps. Rest standardizes its CLI wrapper with consistent quote usage and import ordering. Worker corrects a deviation by reverting inadvertently minified build scripts to readable PascalCase format. Mountain adds native macOS dmg target support, EULA templates, and updated icon assets for the release cycle.\n\nThese changes ensure the editor's build system adheres to project readability standards in development while delivering optimized, deterministic artifacts for production, alongside expanded native distribution capabilities.",
			"SHA": "a43be3f4250cd24c901ed4afac91b4bf3e58f1bd"
